1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:05,074
Deaf and hard-of-hearing people miss the
sounds that matter at home:

2
00:00:05,124 --> 00:00:07,202
the door, the alarm, the baby.

3
00:00:07,252 --> 00:00:10,323
It listens, alerts on its screen and
lights,

4
00:00:10,373 --> 00:00:14,650
and runs entirely on this Alif E8 board.
Nothing is recorded.

5
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,982
Every start runs a self-test of the mics,
the NPU, the

6
00:00:19,032 --> 00:00:22,438
saved sounds, the vibration sensor and the
lights.

7
00:00:22,488 --> 00:00:24,650
Ready in one and a half seconds.

8
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:31,681
In a quiet room the NPU rests to save
power.

9
00:00:31,731 --> 00:00:36,650
When I talk, the encoder wakes up.

10
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:42,164
Seven sounds are built in. Here's an
alarm:

11
00:00:42,214 --> 00:00:47,079
icon, word and time, colour-blind-safe,
and

12
00:00:47,129 --> 00:00:51,650
the lights flash a pattern of their own.

13
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:55,796
Here's what a microphone alone can't do.

14
00:00:55,846 --> 00:01:00,761
I knock on the table, twenty centimetres
from the board.

15
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:05,460
The accelerometer, read eight hundred
times a second,

16
00:01:05,510 --> 00:01:10,691
feels it, and the microphones hear it:
felt here and heard.

17
00:01:10,741 --> 00:01:17,075
Now the same knock from the laptop, held
in the air, like a knock on TV.

18
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:23,990
The microphones hear it, but nothing
touched the table, so it's only a banner:

19
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:26,650
heard only.

20
00:01:27,300 --> 00:01:33,149
Every home sounds different, so you teach
it your own.

21
00:01:33,199 --> 00:01:38,938
Press up, pick a name, here Keys, and
press to start.

22
00:01:38,988 --> 00:01:42,215
I jingle my keys eight times.

23
00:01:42,265 --> 00:01:45,493
Each example is checked:

24
00:01:45,543 --> 00:01:52,811
too quiet, clipped, a loud room, or unlike
the others gets flagged,

25
00:01:52,861 --> 00:01:58,929
and a good one turns green with its level
over the room.

26
00:01:58,979 --> 00:02:02,315
One more jingle tests it. Save.

27
00:02:02,365 --> 00:02:05,592
No laptop and no retraining:

28
00:02:05,642 --> 00:02:12,474
the board builds a profile from the NPU's
embeddings, and saves

29
00:02:12,524 --> 00:02:18,373
it to flash in the background without
missing a sound.

30
00:02:18,423 --> 00:02:21,650
And now it knows my keys.

31
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,625
Now I reset the board.

32
00:02:24,675 --> 00:02:30,404
The self-test restores the taught sounds
from flash, in two milliseconds.

33
00:02:30,454 --> 00:02:33,650
Jingle again, and it still knows my keys.

34
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:47,372
Right shows the numbers, live from the
board:

35
00:02:47,422 --> 00:02:51,742
our own PyTorch model, all fourteen
operators on the Ethos-U85,

36
00:02:51,792 --> 00:02:55,072
about one millisecond per run, and the CPU
awake

37
00:02:55,122 --> 00:02:59,650
twelve point six percent of the time in a
quiet room. Sound Sense.

